WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.800
Conditional aggregation lets one grouped query
calculate several related metrics from the

00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:10.706
same input rows Suppose we want separate counts for
pneumonia and fracture

00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:16.393
admissions for each patient We could run separate
queries but conditional aggregation

00:00:16.419 --> 00:00:21.991
keeps the measures together in one result There are
two common patterns

00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:27.405
in this module CASE is widely portable and can
convert a condition

00:00:27.418 --> 00:00:33.001
into a value that an aggregate can summarize
PostgreSQL FILTER

00:00:33.027 --> 00:00:36.527
attaches a condition directly to an aggregate and is
often easier to

00:00:36.553 --> 00:00:41.754
read when each measure has its own condition The
important idea is

00:00:41.768 --> 00:00:45.268
that the group stays the same while different
subsets of rows contribute

00:00:45.294 --> 00:00:46.307
to different measures
